Reconstruct a sedimentary rock from sources through burial and alteration (@mp-sedimentary-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mineralogy-and-petrology, #source "../sources/MIT-Sedimentary-Geology.lingua#r_7FWZZ66CT5G1FP2JPQMWRV1YHM", #source "../sources/BGS-Rock-Classification-Scheme.lingua#r_0715XKKA34SBMSRTCCZD3KJQEH", #source "../sources/USGS-X-ray-Powder-Diffraction-Manual.lingua#r_3S2AET1HS289HRQBDJ87A30DX6", #source "../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD", #source "../../geology/sources/Introduction-to-Geochronology-Vermeesch.lingua#r_30AEAXYK3VV89FDX1TF9ZKJ84J", #mineralogy-and-petrology "Advanced-metamorphic-model-and-petrochronology-study.lingua#r_7P5KPCH145YG8XYV124C723F73") { r_21K256CCMWD35R663MPV64NG88
**Read:** [Sedimentary Geology — John Southard, MIT 12.110](../sources/MIT-Sedimentary-Geology.lingua#r_7FWZZ66CT5G1FP2JPQMWRV1YHM), the complete notes and full relevant original references; [Rock Classification Scheme — British Geological Survey](../sources/BGS-Rock-Classification-Scheme.lingua#r_0715XKKA34SBMSRTCCZD3KJQEH), the full applicable reports; [A laboratory manual for X-ray powder diffraction — Poppe and colleagues](../sources/USGS-X-ray-Powder-Diffraction-Manual.lingua#r_3S2AET1HS289HRQBDJ87A30DX6), the full relevant analytical method; [Guide to Thin Section Microscopy — Raith, Raase, and Reinhardt](../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD), the full observation/measurement procedures used; [Introduction to Geochronology — Pieter Vermeesch](../../geology/sources/Introduction-to-Geochronology-Vermeesch.lingua#r_30AEAXYK3VV89FDX1TF9ZKJ84J), the full relevant detrital/chronological method.

Choose a clastic, carbonate, evaporitic, siliceous, or other sedimentary-material question with sufficient section/specimen context. Read the complete sedimentary notes and original case/method papers. Connect source, transport/deposition, texture, mineralogy, reactions, fluids, burial, and preservation rather than interpreting each proxy independently.

Produce or reconstruct a documented petrographic description, justified modal/classification account, and chemical/mineralogical measurements. Preserve counting basis, sample selection, unresolved grains, preparation, analytical support, and uncertainty. Identify what was deposited and what formed or changed later.

Reproduce one consequential provenance, mixture, reaction-transfer, chronology, porosity, or diagenetic argument. Independently check quantities and test an alternative involving sorting/recycling, replacement, different fluid history, sampling, or missing phases. State which observations can discriminate it and which merely repeat the same assumption.

**Work:** produce a sustained source-to-burial history supported by maps/sections where relevant, original texture/domain evidence, complete references, reproducible calculation, alternative interpretation, and a feasible next study. Connect one result with groundwater, material quality, or another explicit practical question while identifying additional specialist work needed.

Defend the report against independent critique and revise it with evidence-linked changes. A convenient rock name or normalized compositional triangle is useful communication but insufficient as the project's full explanatory result.

**Continue:** [Defend a metamorphic history with domain, phase, and chronological tests](Advanced-metamorphic-model-and-petrochronology-study.lingua#r_7P5KPCH145YG8XYV124C723F73).

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN).
